        "\n",
        "**Working in Python:** To work in Python, we will use [Google Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/):\n",
        "\n",
        "* Click on the link to go to Colab\n",
        "* Log in with your WFU google account\n",
        "* Click \"New Notebook\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# How likely is 'likely'? Revisited\n",
        "\n",
        "## Motivation\n",
        "\n",
        "In an [online quiz](https://probability.kucharski.io/), created as an independent project by Adam Kucharski, over 5,000 participants compared pairs of probability phrases (e.g. “Which conveys a higher probability: Likely or Probable?”) and assigned numerical values (0–100%) to each of 19 phrases. The resulting data can be used to analyse how people interpret common probability phrases.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Data\n",
        "\n",
        "The code below will download three different datasets:"
      ],
      "id": "da4820a2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "absolute_judgements = pd.read_csv('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rfordatascience/tidytuesday/main/data/2026/2026-03-10/absolute_judgements.csv')\n",
        "pairwise_comparisons = pd.read_csv('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rfordatascience/tidytuesday/main/data/2026/2026-03-10/pairwise_comparisons.csv')\n",
        "respondent_metadata = pd.read_csv('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rfordatascience/tidytuesday/main/data/2026/2026-03-10/respondent_metadata.csv')"
      ],
      "id": "72b71d42",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### `absolute_judgements.csv`\n",
        "\n",
        "In the `absolute_judgements` dataset, respondents provide a numerical value (0-100%) for each different probability phrase (\"Little Change\", \"Almost No Chance\", etc.). These 19 different phrases were presented to each respondent in a random order.\n",
        "\n",
        "|variable    |class     |description                           |\n",
        "|:-----------|:---------|:-------------------------------------|\n",
        "|response_id |integer   |Unique respondent identifier. |\n",
        "|term        |character |Probability phrase. |\n",
        "|probability |integer   |Numerical estimate (0--100). |\n",
        "|order       |integer   |Presentation order of this term for the respondent. |\n",
        "\n",
        "### `pairwise_comparisons.csv`\n",
        "\n",
        "In the `pairwise_comparisons` dataset, respondents were presented with pairs of probability phrases, and asked to decide which phrase indicated higher probability. \n",
        "\n",
        "variable    |class     |description                           |\n",
        "|:-----------|:---------|:-------------------------------------|\n",
        "|response_id |integer   |Unique respondent identifier. |\n",
        "|pair_id     |integer   |Pair sequence number within the respondent's session (1--10). |\n",
        "|term1       |character |First term shown. |\n",
        "|term2       |character |Second term shown. |\n",
        "|selected    |character |The term the respondent chose as higher probability. |\n",
        "\n",
        "### `respondent_metadata.csv`\n",
        "\n",
        "The `respondent_metadata` dataset contains some information on respondent demographics.\n",
        "\n",
        "|variable             |class     |description                           |\n",
        "|:--------------------|:---------|:-------------------------------------|\n",
        "|response_id          |integer   |Unique respondent identifier. |\n",
        "|timestamp            |character |Submission month (YYYY-MM). |\n",
        "|age_band             |character |Self-reported age band (e.g. \"25-34\"). |\n",
        "|english_background   |character |English language background. |\n",
        "|education_level      |character |Highest education level. |\n",
        "|country_of_residence |character |Country of residence. |\n",
        "\n",
        "## Questions\n",
        "\n",
        "Note: this list of [built-in aggregation methods](https://pandas.pydata.org/pandas-docs/stable/user_guide/groupby.html#built-in-aggregation-methods) may be helpful.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Using the `absolute_judgements` dataset, identify the terms which have the highest and lowest average probability. \n",
        "\n",
        "2. Using the `absolute_judgements` dataset, identify the terms which have the highest and lowest variability in the response probabilities. On which terms do the respondents most agree? Disagree?\n",
        "\n",
        "3. Using the `absolute_judgements` dataset, count the number of unique terms for each participant. Did every participant respond to 19 questions?\n",
        "\n",
        "### Joining datasets\n",
        "\n",
        "Read the [introduction](https://pandas.pydata.org/pandas-docs/stable/user_guide/merging.html#merge) to the `merge` method in `pandas`. Then answer the following question.\n",
        "\n",
        "4. Merge the `absolute_judgements` and `response_metadata` datasets, and use the resulting dataset to compute the average probability for each age band. Which age band is most \"optimistic\"?\n"
      ],
      "id": "661cb4b1"
    }
